<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The hardened-runtime entitlements of Wanderbooks.app (plan P15 unit C1).

     The app is signed with the hardened runtime (codesign --options
     runtime), which Apple's notarization requires. It is NOT sandboxed
     (the App Sandbox would forbid what the product is: it starts a copy of
     itself as the books server, runs the system's git for backups, and
     reads and writes the person's data folder and the folders they pick
     for backups). Outside the sandbox, none of that needs an entitlement:

       * starting itself as a child process and git as another: none;
       * outgoing network connections (the relay, the update look, a git
         remote): none (com.apple.security.network.client is a SANDBOX
         entitlement);
       * reading and writing its data folder, Application Support/wanderbooks:
         none (the Documents folder is a privacy prompt, answered by
         NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription in Info.plist, not an entitlement);
       * the window's graphics (Metal through wgpu): none;
       * no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no DYLD variables, no
         library validation exception: the program loads only system
         frameworks and its own code.

     So the set below is empty on purpose. If the first notarized build
     fails to start, the log names the entitlement it needs; add exactly
     that one here, with the reason, and not a broader exception. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
